# Modular STM32 Teaching State

This module implements the editable Teaching state for a multi-segment robot
program. It uses fixed-size storage, no heap allocation, no STM32 HAL calls and
no MATLAB dependencies.

## Ownership boundary

- `TeachingState` owns the editable state, working segment and draft program.
- `TeachingInputs` is a coherent read-only snapshot owned by motion, safety,
  drive, kinematics and configuration modules.
- `TeachingOutputs` provides HMI information and a one-cycle validation request.
- Path Validation—not Teaching—runs geometry generation, arc-length
  parameterization, time scaling, IK, FK checking, limits and collision checks.

For a recorded line, Path Validation maps:

```text
P_start        = segment.points[0].position_m
P_end          = segment.points[1].position_m
R_start/end    = quaternion-derived orientations
desired speed  = segment.speed_mps * program.global_speed_scale
initial IK seed= segment.points[0].joint_position_rad
```

That interface is compatible with the conceptual inputs of the MATLAB line
trajectory pipeline without embedding the pipeline inside this state.

## Reset semantics

`TEACH_EVENT_RESET` immediately erases the RAM draft and working segment. It:

- requires no confirmation;
- does not command motion or homing;
- does not clear E-stop, protective-stop or global fault ownership;
- increments the draft revision so an older validation result cannot match.

The operational Reset HMI input must not be connected directly to the STM32
`NRST` pin. It must arrive as a debounced, edge-triggered software event.

## Debug output

For a desktop test:

```sh
cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic \
  -DTEACHING_DEBUG_ENABLE=1 \
  teaching_state.c teaching_state_test.c -lm -o teaching_state_test
./teaching_state_test
```

For STM32, define `TEACHING_DEBUG_PRINTF` as the project logger before including
`teaching_debug.h`. Prefer buffered UART DMA, SWO/ITM or SEGGER RTT. Disable
debug logs in the real-time release build.

## Integration loop

1. Debounce the physical/HMI inputs and create one edge-triggered event.
2. Build one coherent `TeachingInputs` snapshot.
3. Call `TeachingState_ProcessEvent()` from the supervisory task—not an ISR.
4. Translate `status_message_id` into Arabic or English in the HMI module.
5. When `validation_request` pulses, deep-copy or transfer the frozen draft to
   Path Validation and transition out of Teaching.

The caller should serialize access if the two STM32H745 cores can access the
same draft. A single owner core plus mailbox/message passing is preferred over
both cores writing the structure.

## Suggested STM32 project placement

```text
Core/Inc/teaching_state.h
Core/Inc/teaching_state_types.h
Core/Inc/teaching_debug.h
Core/Src/teaching_state.c
```

`stm32_integration_example.c` is deliberately excluded with `#if 0`; it shows
the supervisory-task connection points without assuming a particular HAL,
RTOS, HMI transport or dual-core allocation.

